  "independentlyComputedDifferences": [
    {
      "language": "zh",
      "pointer": "/prose/0/text",
      "before": "原书用电子管振荡器说明调幅：改变电子管两极（例如阳极与阴极）之间的电位差，可以调节其产生的高频电振荡的振幅。\n在所述电路的适用工作范围内，阳极与阴极间的电压增大时，阳极电流以及电源在一个周期内向振荡回路输送的能量通常随之增大，回路中的电振荡振幅也相应增大。\n阳极电压降低时，输入回路的能量和振幅相应减小。\n\n这是该电路的工作关系，不是任意电子管在任何工作状态下都成立的无条件规律。",
      "after": "原书用电子管振荡器说明调幅：改变电子管两极（例如阳极与阴极）之间的电位差，可以调节其产生的高频电振荡的振幅。\n在所述电路的适用工作范围内，该三极管的阳极与阴极间的电压增大时，阳极电流以及电源在一个周期内向振荡回路输送的能量通常随之增大，回路中的电振荡振幅也相应增大。\n阳极电压降低时，输入回路的能量和振幅相应减小。\n\n这是该电路的工作关系，不是任意电子管在任何工作状态下都成立的无条件规律。",
      "exactSubstitution": {
        "from": "在所述电路的适用工作范围内，阳极与阴极间的电压增大时",
        "to": "在所述电路的适用工作范围内，该三极管的阳极与阴极间的电压增大时"
      }
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "pointer": "/prose/0/text",
      "before": "The textbook uses a vacuum-tube oscillator to illustrate amplitude modulation: changing the potential difference between two tube electrodes, such as the anode and cathode, can adjust the amplitude of its high-frequency electrical oscillations. Within the operating range assumed for this circuit, an increase in anode-to-cathode voltage generally increases the anode current and the energy supplied by the power source to the oscillatory circuit during one period, with a corresponding increase in oscillation amplitude. When the anode voltage decreases, the energy supplied to the circuit and the amplitude decrease correspondingly. This describes the operation of this circuit, not an unconditional rule for every tube in every operating state.",
      "after": "The textbook uses a vacuum-tube oscillator to illustrate amplitude modulation: changing the potential difference between two tube electrodes, such as the anode and cathode, can adjust the amplitude of its high-frequency electrical oscillations. Within the operating range assumed for this circuit, an increase in the triode's anode-to-cathode voltage generally increases the anode current and the energy supplied by the power source to the oscillatory circuit during one period, with a corresponding increase in oscillation amplitude. When the anode voltage decreases, the energy supplied to the circuit and the amplitude decrease correspondingly. This describes the operation of this circuit, not an unconditional rule for every tube in every operating state.",
      "exactSubstitution": {
        "from": "an increase in anode-to-cathode voltage generally increases the anode current",
        "to": "an increase in the triode's anode-to-cathode voltage generally increases the anode current"
      }
    }
